        <COMMENT ADDRESS="1000:0118" TYPE="pre">The MDA (Monochrome Display Adapter) decodes a 32KB region from B000:0000 to B7FF:000F, though only the first 4KB is actual video RAM (mirrored through the full range). This region is present only when an MDA card is installed. On systems with a CGA or VGA adapter but no MDA, this region is typically unmapped and free for use.</COMMENT>
